 "title": "Biofilm Formation and Nutrient Availability in Bacteria",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the formation of biofilms by bacteria, specifically E. coli and B. subtilis, and their impact on nutrient availability. Biofilms are composed of curli fibers, which are produced by E. coli and contribute to the formation of biofilms. The presence of biofilms influences nutrient availability, and curli amyloid fibers affect this process. The formation of biofilms also involves the production of matrix and the supply of nutrients by E. coli. Various methods and tools, such as ThioT, Curli fiber, and Direct Red, are used to study and quantify biofilms and their components.",
